From 933ec16a83c2433d6bdda074fb0132a37d58f250 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vignesh Sridharan <vignsrid@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 22:12:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] agent: Add SMD capability detection and propagation

Implement end-to-end SMD capability detection from NL80211 driver
through to Agent database and QCA vendor TLV reporting.

Changes include:
- Define NL80211_ATTR_SMD_SUPPORT (382) and NL80211_ATTR_SMD_STA_DL_DATA_FWD
  (386) locally via #ifndef guards, as these are QCA vendor extensions not
  yet in the upstream kernel nl80211.h
- Read SMD support and DL data forwarding flags from NL80211 wiphy
  attributes and propagate through BWL HAL layer (RadioInfo)
- Add smd_support and smd_dl_data_fwd_support fields to sNodeHostap
  message structure and pack them in ACTION_APMANAGER_JOINED_NOTIFICATION
- Store SMD capabilities in AgentDB sRadio structure
- Add set_qca_agent_smd_capabilities() helper in multi_vendor_qca.cpp
  to pass aggregated SMD capabilities to the QCA TLV handler
- Replace hardcoded 0x80 in add_qca_smd_capabilities_tlv() with actual
  values from AgentDB, aggregated across all radios (OR operation)
- Set SMD capabilities before add_vs_tlv() only for
  EARLY_AP_CAPABILITY_REPORT_MESSAGE, where the TLV is registered

Signed-off-by: Vignesh Sridharan <vignsrid@qti.qualcomm.com>
